module gunbc.rung_drop.owner_deletion_follow_up_charge_removed

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.rung_drop { RungDrop, Standing, TypedDeclaration, DeletedWithoutReplacement }
import gunbc.guarantee_rung { MechanicallyPreventable, Mitigatable }

// POPULATION EMPTY, DROP NOT RETIRED (2026-09-19, gunbc#11704). Transition admissions are now
// carried in the commit messages of the change that needs them and TransitionAdmission no longer
// has a deletion_follow_up field, so no row can be in this drop's population: the used rows whose
// owner authored no deletion_follow_up. RECEIPT: v1_compiler.namespace_wave_admission
// tree_carried_admission_refusal refuses any row file in the tree, and the type in
// gunbc.namespace.transition_admission carries only label, subject and disposition. The drop is
// INERT, NOT RETIRED: DESIGN section 4b(3) retires a drop by its trigger and by nothing else, and
// this row's trigger -- resolving an authored follow-up number to the pull request it names -- has
// not fired. The declaration below is kept verbatim as the record of what was true on 2026-09-16.
//
// DECLARED 2026-09-16 beside gunbc#11481, which removed BOTH merge_group follow-up arms of
// wave_admission_refusal on an operator ruling that mandating a deletion follow-up pull request is
// not worth its cost. The sibling row consumed_row_owner_charge_unenforced covers the removal of
// ConsumedRowOwnerChargeBypassed. THIS ROW COVERS THE OTHER ONE, OwnerFollowUpAbsent, WHICH AN
// EARLIER REVISION OF THAT CHANGE MISCLASSIFIED AS A DECORATION AND THEREFORE DID NOT DECLARE.
//
// WHY THAT CLASSIFICATION WAS WRONG (review 67014). DESIGN section 4b defines a decoration as a
// check whose forbidden state cannot be expressed anywhere the check could run -- permanently green
// BY CONSTRUCTION. OwnerFollowUpAbsent was not that. Its forbidden state was expressible and was
// refused, by a test in src/v1/stage0/tests/namespace_wave_admission.rs that is still enrolled on
// this branch, inverted to assert the arm is gone. That its GREEN
// established only the weaker property -- that digits were typed, never that they name an open or
// deleting pull request -- LOWERS THE CLASS THE CHECK COVERED. It does not make the check
// permanently green, and a weak wall is still a wall: removing it drops the narrow class -- an
// owner lands a used row carrying no follow-up number at all -- from mechanically preventable.
//
// SO TWO CLASSES FELL, AND THEY GET TWO ROWS RATHER THAN ONE WIDENED POPULATION, BECAUSE THEIR
// RESTORATION TRIGGERS DIFFER. The sibling's coverage returns when a required run can adjudicate a
// consumed row at all; this one's returns only when the charge is worth making -- see the trigger.

data owner_deletion_follow_up_charge_removed: RungDrop = RungDrop {
  identity: "owner_deletion_follow_up_charge_removed" as NonEmptyStr,

  subject: "a used transition-admission row carrying no deletion_follow_up is refused on the required run of the very change that uses it",

  declared: "2026-09-16",

  amendments: [],

  standing: Standing,

  declaration: TypedDeclaration {
    previous: MechanicallyPreventable,
    temporary: Mitigatable,
    reason: DeletedWithoutReplacement,
    population: [
      "used transition-admission rows whose owning change authored no deletion_follow_up, on that owning change's own merge_group composition -- EMPTY since gunbc#11704, which deleted the field"
    ],
    restoration_trigger: "THE CAPABILITY: a required run that adjudicates a deletion_follow_up against WHAT IT NAMES -- resolving the authored number to a pull request that exists and is open or deleting the row -- rather than against the fact that digits were typed. Nothing smaller retires this row, AND IN PARTICULAR RE-ADDING THE REMOVED ARM DOES NOT. That arm's admitting side was satisfied by any digits, so restoring it would restore an advance commitment nobody can check while charging every owner for it, which is the cost the operator ruling priced out; the coverage that is missing is not the refusal but the referent behind it. Nor does authoring follow-up numbers on the rows standing today, which changes the population and not the coverage. What remained from 2026-09-16 was a RECORD and not a refusal -- deletion_follow_up carried on every row and used_without_follow_up counted in the refusal message. SINCE gunbc#11704 (2026-09-19) NEITHER EXISTS: transition admissions are carried in the commit messages of the change that needs them, TransitionAdmission has no deletion_follow_up field, and WaveAdmissionReport has no used_without_follow_up, so this drop's population is EMPTY and no record of it remains. The drop stays Standing because the trigger above has not fired; it is inert, not retired.",
  }
}
